  noteContent: I put a particle in two places at once near a black hole's event horizon.
    The black hole's gravity alone could "measure" which path it takes by absorbing
    information through soft gravitons. This forces the superposition to collapse
    before any human looks. The black hole doesn't need eyes, its presence alone
    acts as the universe's most final observer.
